te and delays."},"controlledInstallation":{"title":"Controlled Installation","description":"Execution follows coordinated sequences, technical details, and inspection-based quality control."},"finalVerification":{"title":"Final Verification","description":"The delivered system is checked against execution quality, waterproofing details, and project requirements."}}},"caseStudies":{"eyebrow":"Project Proof","title":"Case studies with measurable engineering context","cta":"Explore Proven Projects","challenge":"Challenge","engineeringDecision":"Engineering Decision","measuredResult":"Measured Result"},"comparison":{"title":"Supply-Only vs Engineering-Controlled Execution","columns":{"supplyOnly":"Typical Supply-Only Approach","sipanel":"SIPANEL Engineering-Controlled Approach"},"points":{"panelSelection":{"label":"Panel selection","typical":"Panel type may be selected mainly from availability or price, with limited review of site constraints.","sipanel":"Panel selection is checked against building use, roof geometry, insulation needs, and execution risk."},"waterproofingResponsibility":{"label":"Waterproofing responsibility","typical":"Waterproofing details may be left to site interpretation during installation.","sipanel":"Drainage, flashing, overlap, and sealing logic are coordinated before execution to reduce leakage risk."},"materialWaste":{"label":"Material waste","typical":"Quantities can be ordered before panel layout and accessory coordination are fully resolved.","sipanel":"Procurement follows coordinated layouts and material planning to support waste control."},"installationCoordination":{"label":"Installation coordination","typical":"Installers may resolve sequence and alignment issues directly on site.","sipanel":"Installation follows planned sequencing, alignment checkpoints, and coordinated technical details."},"riskBeforeConstruction":{"label":"Risk before construction","typical":"Project risks often become visible after materials arrive or installation 